{
  "info": {
    "name": "OpenAgriNet - V1 on the V2 network",
    "description": "Drive the local stack that answers a Beckn V1 request out of the V2\nnetwork, with BharatVistaar unchanged.\n\n    V1 caller --search--> V1 adapter --select--> V2 adapter --GET--> Mausamgram\n                :3001                   :3002                 :9100\n\nBoth adapters are the same beckn-onix binary with different configs. V2 is\nwhat travels between them; V1 never leaves the outer edges.\n\nBefore running anything:\n\n    cd docs/migration-design/local-stack\n    docker compose up -d\n    cd v1-adapter && ./up.sh\n\nThen run folder 0, then folder 1. Stop with ./down.sh.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Is everything up",
      "description": "Run these first if anything below misbehaves. The adapters are started by\n../v1-adapter/up.sh and the other two by docker compose, so a failure here\ntells you which of the two you forgot.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "V1 adapter",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{v1Adapter}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{v1Adapter}}/health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Started by ../v1-adapter/up.sh."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('up', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
