    {
      "name": "4. What the adapters read from the registry",
      "description": "Every field the adapters look up, and nothing else. Useful for seeing how\nlittle a row has to carry for a capability to be reachable, and for seeing\nthat the two hops are the same mechanism one level apart.\n\nThese are POSTs with a filter body, which is the shape sunbirdRegistry sends.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "the V2 adapter, as the V1 adapter sees it",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"participantId\": {\n      \"eq\": \"WFC\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{registry}}/api/v1/Participant/search",
              "host": [
                "{{registry}}/api/v1/Participant/search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The V1 adapter resolves its upstream here. baseUrl in this row is what\nmakes the V2 adapter reachable, so the hop is configuration and not code.\n\nparticipantId is WFC, the capability's own code, because a V1 payload\nnames no participant for the left half of a binding key to come from."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('one row', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.lengthOf(1));",
                  "pm.test('points at the V2 adapter', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()[0].baseUrl).to.include('3002'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Mausamgram, as the V2 adapter sees it",
